<p>Ukraine said it struck Russia’s Baltic Sea port of Primorsk and several Russian vessels on Sunday, including a Karakurt-class missile ship, a patrol boat and tankers Kyiv says are part of Moscow’s “shadow fleet” used to move sanctioned oil. President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Ukrainian forces also hit two shadow fleet tankers near the entrance to the Black Sea port of Novorossiysk, and he posted footage of a naval drone approaching one tanker. Alexander Drozdenko, governor of Russia’s Leningrad region, confirmed a fire at Primorsk after the drone attack and said there was no oil spill; Russian authorities said air defenses downed more than 60 drones over the region overnight. Primorsk, operated by Russia’s state oil pipeline company Transneft, is one of Russia’s largest oil export gateways and has capacity of about 1 million barrels per day. The attacks came during another large overnight exchange of drones. Kyiv’s air force said Russia launched 268 drones and one ballistic missile at Ukraine, while Moscow’s defense ministry said Ukraine launched at least 334 drones at Russia. Casualty counts differed across accounts: AFP-based reports said at least eight people were killed in both countries, while BBC reported 10 people killed by Russian strikes around Ukraine.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/2PLI4CehpTwlAduWLTGoAKamh0HRkivRlLSUEmGSD2fFwqIqTCwQnU2baYhyKRMHZeTCUm7XkwJo3gdyLLo9oVf1a3YcyrhWZh87flL6ml4gjyCR9hX590EWneUfm9Mz2w' alt='Ukrainian footage shows an attack on two tankers near Novorossiysk on May 3, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Kyiv’s rationale: Kyiv said its strikes on Russian targets were a response to recent Russian bombardments of Ukrainian cities.</li><li>Moscow region: A Ukrainian drone attack killed a 77-year-old man in the Moscow region, and Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin said four drones were shot down on their way to the capital.</li><li>Zelenskyy’s warning: Zelenskyy said Russia could end the war at any time and that prolonging it would expand Ukraine’s defensive operations.</li><li>Eastern front: Ukraine’s top army official said Russian troops were moving toward Kostiantynivka in the eastern Donetsk region.</li></ul><blockquote>These tankers had been actively used to transport oil – not anymore - Volodymyr Zelenskyy</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Volodymyr Zelenskyy: Zelenskyy described the strikes as Ukraine “applying sanctions” against Russia’s oil fleet and said Ukraine would keep developing long-range capabilities at sea, in the air and on land. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458053/russias-primorsk-port-hit-as-ukraine-launches-wave-of-drone-strikes'>Aaj TV</a>)</li><li>Alexander Drozdenko: The Leningrad regional governor did not immediately give further details about casualties or the extent of damage at Primorsk beyond acknowledging the incident. (<a href='https://www.wwaytv3.com/ukraine-hits-key-russian-oil-loading-port-and-3-shadow-fleet-tankers/'>WWAY TV3</a>)</li><li>Dmitry Peskov: The Kremlin spokesman said attacks on oil infrastructure could push oil prices higher and increase Russian revenue. (<a href='https://www.avgi.gr/diethni/521630_kyma-oykranikon-epitheseon-se-rosikes-petrelaikes-ypodomes-kai-dexamenoploia'>Avgi</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ukraine-russia-war-strikes-shadow-fleet-oil-infrastructure/'>Ukraine hits Russian oil assets, including &quot;shadow fleet&quot; tankers</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1997347/kyiv-hits-russian-oil-sites-as-8-killed-in-both-countries'>Kyiv hits Russian oil sites as 8 killed in both countries</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/russian-strike-kills-one-as-ukraine-launches-hundreds-of-drones/article70934520.ece'>Russia, Ukraine drones kill four; hit ‘shadow fleet’ tankers</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://thisday.com.ng/ukraine-hits-key-russian-oil-loading-port-and-3-shadow-fleet-tankers/'>U